##1356. Sort Integers by The Number of 1 Bits
##Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/sort-integers-by-the-number-of-1-bits/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-02-25
##Intuition:
We are sorting based on two conditions:

First priority → number of 1s in binary (bit count)

Second priority → numeric value (ascending)

So each number has a key pair like this:

(number of 1s, actual number)

Then we sort by:

smaller bit count first

if equal → smaller number first

#We can convert number to binary and count:num.toString(2)
##Time Complexity:
Sorting → O(n log n)
Bit counting per comparison → O(log maxValue)
Overall → O(n log n)



/**
 * @param {number[]} arr
 * @return {number[]}
 */
var sortByBits = function(arr) {
    return arr.sort((a,b)=>{
        let bitsa=a.toString(2).split("1").length-1;
        let bitsb=b.toString(2).split("1").length-1;
        if(bitsa===bitsb)return a-b;
        return bitsa-bitsb;
    })
};
